{
  "$comment": "A saved tank checked as the site's tank-mates tool checks the fish chosen there (apps/site/src/scripts/tank-check.ts, from tankmates.ts, stocking.ts and calc.ts). The site's tests run that code on these cases, and the iOS app's tests run the same code bundled (apps/ios/AquaTomeKit/Sources/TankCheck/tank-check.js) in JavaScriptCore: both must answer `check` exactly. `fish`: the tank's rows, each one's name and tank-mates figures as the app index gives them, and `count` when the tank has one; `key`, what the check counts the row as (the page's content id, or a breed's species: the app index's `of ?? id`, the row then carrying the species' figures and, as `species`, its name). Rows with one key are one fish, named as the row when it is alone and as the species when there are more, counted as their numbers added up, at least the school size when a row gives none, and as none when none does (`oneFishEach`). `size`: the tank's inside size (cm) and its own litres, either or both. `unlisted`: the names of the tank's fish without a page (its entries without one), which no check counts; `check.unchecked` names them.",
